 26 // heldIdentity reads the identity while p holds the process. On Linux 5.4 and
 27 // later os.FindProcess opened a pidfd, so a PID reused after that cannot receive
 28 // the signal: the stamp read here belongs to the PID's holder at this instant,
 29 // which is p's process or a newcomer, and a newcomer reads as another stamp.
 30 func heldIdentity(_ *os.Process, pid int) (uint64, error) { return readIdentity(pid) }
 31 
 32 // isNoSuchProcess never holds on Linux: os.FindProcess does not fail there.
 33 func isNoSuchProcess(error) bool { return false }
